  "note": "Municipal elections, 20 May 1964. The seven elected and their votes are from the Belfast Telegraph's provincial results table (21 May 1964, p. 4), read from the page image. The Telegraph names seven defeated candidates without votes; the Irish News (22 May 1964, p. 7) prints the same figures for the elected and the votes of eight defeated candidates, which are recorded here: Peter Donnelly 279, Peter P. Finnegan 275, Mrs. Bridget McAleer 275 (printed 'McAeer'; the Telegraph has 'Mrs. P. McAleer'), James Mackle 229, Mrs. Angela McCrystal 191, Malachy Sweeney 152, Jas. McGivern 137 and Patrick F. Woods (Ratepayers) 10, who had dropped out through illness but stayed on the ballot. The Irish News gives the elected as P. G. McQuaid, Mrs. Patricia McCuskey [sic], T. J. Donaghy and Patrick McCooey where the Telegraph has D. J. McQuaid, Patricia McCluskey, P. J. Donaghy and F. McCooey; the Telegraph's forms are kept.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page images of Belfast Telegraph, 21 May 1964, p. 4 and Irish News, 22 May 1964, p. 7 (council-audit, Nov 2026): 'F. McCooley' corrected to F. McCooey as printed; eight defeated candidates added with their votes from the Irish News."
